// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - MedicalPaperwork 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P4209504499" "Medical Paperwork"
// DetailString :
"P911403072" "This paperwork certifies that Dr. Steffard gives his professional medical opinion that you are ready for combat. There is also a scribbled stick figure diagram on the side that looks somewhat like you defeating a clockwork."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - DrSteffardDialog 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro Text :
"P1109893659" "Hello. I'm Dr. Steffard, you must be the new recruit.<br><br>Ah, here you are.  {HeroName}, a {Hero.gender=Male powerful|lovely} {HeroClass}.  I saw you demolish that robot with great panache!  Impressive.<br><br>My research on super powered individuals is indeed extensive, my resume vast, I have extrapolated theoretical super powered beings that were then found to exist in the wild!<br><br>My theories on {HeroOrigin} supers of course predicted you could exist; so I know everything about how your powers work.  I..."
// Answer Text :
"P2596766879" "I'm in a bit of a hurry. Could you sign these papers?"
// Answer Text :
"P1836456449" "(Optional Help) The Interrogator said you could tell me more about my powers."
// Answer Text :
"P3828289715" "(Optional Help) These powers are a mess, I need organization!"
// Answer Text :
"P833981879" "(Optional Help) How do I not die while 'defending the peace'?"
// Page PowersInfoBlaster Text :
"P2033040739" "Your {HeroOrigin} powers are just {Hero.gender=Male sparking|budding} right now.<br><br>For instance, as a <color red>Blaster</color>, you can still use the first two powers of your primary set and the first power of your secondary set while you are held, stunned, or slept. Additionally, whenever you hit with a power, you gain a stacking damage bonus to subsequent attacks for short time.<br><br><color orange>You can right click powers in your power tray or buffs below your status bar to learn more."
// Answer Text :
"P1036764897" "Thanks for the referesher, doc. I'll be on my way now."
// Answer Text :
"P1467300663" "(Optional Help) But these powers are a mess, I need organization!"
// Answer Text :
"P2971377108" "(Optional Help) So how do I not die while 'defending the peace'?"
// Page PowersInfoDominator Text :
"P3089454489" "Your {HeroOrigin} powers are just {Hero.gender=Male sparking|budding} right now.<br><br>For instance, as a <color mediumvioletred>Dominator</color>, some of your stronger foes will be resistant to your control powers and you may have to use a power multiple times before it affects that foe. But when your Domination bar is over 90%, you can activate your <color mediumvioletred>Domination</color> power, doubling the magnitude of your control powers and making it easier to lock down enemies for even longer, as well as refilling your <color dodgerblue>endurance</color> and breaking you free from control effects that are on you.<color orange><br><span align=center><img src=Tut_P_DominationBar.tga></span><br><color orange>You can right click powers in your power tray or buffs below your status bar to learn more."
// Page PowersInfoBrute Text :
"P105496911" "Your {HeroOrigin} powers are just {Hero.gender=Male sparking|budding} right now.<br><br>For instance, as a <color steelblue>Brute</color>, your <color darkorange>FURY</color> increases your attack power. Your fury bar increases the more you attack and get attacked.<br><br><img src=Tut_P_Ragebar.tga><br></span><color orange>You can right click powers in your power tray or buffs below your status bar to learn more."
// Page PowersInfoTanker Text :
"P1657629993" "Your {HeroOrigin} powers are just {Hero.gender=Male sparking|budding} right now.<br><br>For instance, as a <color lightsteelblue>Tanker</color>, you're the the frontline of defense on teams. Your inherent Gauntlet power will draw enemies to attack you with each attack you deliver.<br><br>Additionally, you have the ability to <color red>bruise</color> foes hit by your very first secondary power. <color red>Bruising</color> causes a foe to have a lower resistance to damage for 10 seconds.  However, multiple applications of this debuff will not stack on a single foe.<br><br><color orange>You can right click powers in your power tray or buffs below your status bar to learn more."
// Page PowersInfoMastermind Text :
"P2474633379" "Your {HeroOrigin} powers are just {Hero.gender=Male sparking|budding} right now.<br><br>For instance, as a <color chartreuse>Mastermind</color>, you can not only summon other creatures to do your bidding, but you also have special powers to help control your henchmen. Additionally, if you have line of sight to your underlings and they are within 60 feet, they gain a bonus to accuracy and damage.<br><br>You can set any of your minions to Bodyguard by right-clicking them, selecting the Defensive stance and then using the Follow, Goto, or Stay order. This causes your pets to absorb some of the damage you take.  Also, using the Heel power will prevent your pets from attacking foes you do not wish to engage.<br><br>You also have heals and buffs you can use on your pets and allies and sometimes on yourself, and debuffs you can use on enemies.  Making maximum use of all your powers will enable your team to excel together beyond what you could accomplish alone.<br><br><color orange>You can right click powers in your power tray or buffs below your status bar to learn more."
// Page PowersInfoController Text :
"P3716489761" "Your {HeroOrigin} powers are just {Hero.gender=Male sparking|budding} right now.<br><br>For instance, as a <color magenta>Controller</color>, your control powers let you keep your foes from operating at their maximum efficiency. However, some of your stronger foes will be resistant to your control powers and you may have to use a power multiple times before it affects that foe. Also, whenever you have a foe held, immobilized, slept, or stunned, you deal additional damage to that foe.<br><br>You also have heals and buffs you can use on your allies and sometimes on yourself, and debuffs you can use on enemies.  Making maximum use of all your powers will enable your team to excel together beyond what you could accomplish alone.<br><br><color orange>You can right click powers in your power tray or buffs below your status bar to learn more."
// Page PowersInfoDefender Text :
"P1238561323" "Your {HeroOrigin} powers are just {Hero.gender=Male sparking|budding} right now.<br><br>For instance, as a <color dodgerblue>Defender</color> while you are working with a team, you can use your powers at a decreased <color dodgerblue>endurance</color> cost if your allies are badly damaged.  Conversely, the smaller the team you are on, the greater damage you are able to do.<br><br>You also have heals and buffs you can use on your allies and sometimes on yourself, and debuffs you can use on enemies.  Making maximum use of all your powers will enable your team to excel together beyond what you could accomplish alone.<br><br><color orange>You can right click powers in your power tray or buffs below your status bar to learn more."
// Page PowersInfoCorruptor Text :
"P3099730395" "Your {HeroOrigin} powers are just {Hero.gender=Male sparking|budding} right now.<br><br>For instance, as a <color crimson>Corruptor</color>, you have the Scourge ability.  When a foe has 50% health or less, you gain a chance of dealing double damage with every attack.<br><br>You also have heals and buffs you can use on your allies and sometimes on yourself, and debuffs you can use on enemies.  Making maximum use of all your powers will enable your team to excel together beyond what you could accomplish alone.<br><br><color orange>You can right click powers in your power tray or buffs below your status bar to learn more."
// Page PowersInfoScrapper Text :
"P1441958091" "Your {HeroOrigin} powers are just {Hero.gender=Male sparking|budding} right now.  For instance, you have a 5% chance to deal double damage against any target when using your <color orange>Scrapper</color> attacks.  This chance increases to 10% against Lieutenants, Bosses and stronger foes.<br><br><color orange>You can right click powers in your power tray or buffs below your status bar to learn more."
// Answer Text :
"P436560363" "(Optional Help) That's all well, but my powers tray is disorganized."
// Page PowersInfoStalker Text :
"P1950026705" "Your {HeroOrigin} powers are just {Hero.gender=Male sparking|budding} right now. For instance, if you haven't already turned on your <color lightslategray>Hide</color> power, I would do so now. Whenever you are in a threatening situation, Hide should be on. Hide lets you make <color red>critical hits</color> on targets that are unaware of you and lets you <color lightslategray>avoid detection</color> before you are ready to strike.<br><br>Be careful: taking damage or making attacks will allow others to detect you and temporarily cancel your hide.  You can tell you are hidden by looking under your status bar for the word <color green><b>Hidden</b></color>.<br><br><color orange>You can right click powers in your power tray or buffs below your status bar to learn more."
// Page PowersTab Text :
"P665343245" "You can click the powers tab above the tray to drag new powers to the tray. You can reorganize the powers in your tray by dragging the icons around.<br><img src=Tut_P_PowersTrayOpen.tga>"
// Answer Text :
"P982955621" "That's much better. Can you sign my papers now?"
// Answer Text :
"P2163937456" "(Optional Help) Ah, that helps. So how do I not die while 'defending the peace'?"
// Page Medicom Text :
"P3495203506" "Ah, do not worry.  When you joined the Powers Division, you were tagged by the <color orange>Medicom</color>.<br><br>The Medicom monitors your current medical status at all times, and if you are defeated, it can instantly transport you to the nearest medical facility where you will enjoy a speedy recovery.<br><br>Of course, if you have a nearby associate who can revive you, you can wait for that instead by just <color red>not clicking</color> <color red>Go to Hospital</color>.<br><span align=center><img src=Tut_P_GotoHospital.tga>"
// Answer Text :
"P239052739" "What a relief. I really should be going."
// Answer Text :
"P3113485321" "(Optional) Glad to hear it. How reliable are these Medicoms?"
// Page SendToInterrogator Text :
"P1591388930" "Quite reliable.  Why, once you have had a Medicom frequency applied to you, it cannot be undone.  So no matter what, even if you left the Powers Division, you would still be covered.<br><br>...Of course if you traveled to another dimension or something, it probably wouldn't work.  Unless they somehow had an identical Medicom system.  But that's highly unlikely unless that dimension was a near-mirror of this one.<br><br>Some people surmise that these devices are so advanced that they must be alien technology!  This is nonsense, as the technology was developed by Dr. Keyes himself, a brilliant...<br><br>...<br><br>Sorry, here I am talking away at you, you should probably be heading over to <color orange>Reese</color> to start your mission.  Make sure you take these papers, they have your medical clearance that you are combat ready.<br><br><color orange>You just got a Clue!  To read your clues, click on 'Clues' at the bottom of your compass."
// Answer Text :
"P4060782435" "Leave"
// Page JustSignThePapers Text :
"P3821824958" "Sorry, here I am talking away at you, you should probably be heading over to <color orange>Reese</color> to get your mission.  Make sure you take these papers, they have your medical clearance that you are combat ready.<br><br><color orange>You just got a Clue!  To read your clues, click on 'Clues' at the bottom of your compass."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - HoffmanDialog 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro Text :
"P627404560" "Hello {HeroName}, glad to have you on our side. I will be in charge of getting you combat ready.<br><br>Show me what you've got. Test out your powers on one of these broken clockwork <b>target dummies</b>.<br><br><color orange>Click on a clockwork or hit the <color lawngreen>Tab key</color> to select it, then hit F to get in range.<br><br>You can click on the powers in your tray to activate them.</color><span align=center><img src=Tut_P_Tray_small.tga></span>"
// Answer Text :
"P1177941730" "Sounds like fun."
// Answer Text :
"P2208595181" "(Optional) What's wrong with these clockwork?"
// Page ResistanceClockwork Text :
"P1890449668" "The Resistance sometimes hacks our clockwork and turns them against us. I have a few clockwork here that were reclaimed from the Resistance. Unfortunately, in my attempt to retrieve data from them, they seized up into this malfunctioning mode that wiped their memory.<br><br>They're useless now."
// Answer Text :
"P4087439994" "I have a great use for them. Target practice."
// Page DefeatedClockwork Text :
"P637720512" "Nice one.  I'd say you're ready.  Get yourself over to <color yellow>Dr. Steffard</color>, he'll tell you more about how to use your powers.<br><br>He's not far, just up the street to my right here."
// Answer Text :
"P4187087110" "Okay, thanks."
// Answer Text :
"P2331900062" "(Optional Help) I can't attack fast enough."
// Answer Text :
"P1769772039" "(Optional Help) These guys are real pushovers."
// Page TalkAboutRecharge Text :
"P3756534003" "You can't just attack non-stop.  That's because all powers have a recharge time.<br><br>When you use a power, it goes dark until it recharges.  If you attempt to use it before it finishes recharging, you will queue it up for use as your next attack.<br><br>The simple powers you have right now have relatively short recharge times.  Powers you earn later in your career are more powerful, but take longer to recharge.<br><br><span align=center><img src=Tut_P_PowerRecharging.tga>"
// Answer Text :
"P416843601" "Ok, I get it. I think I'm ready for some action."
// Page TalkAboutConning Text :
"P4139598214" "True, but you will meet tougher enemies. There are three basic ranks:<br><br><b>Minions</b>, like these, are the weakest and are easiest to defeat.<br><b><color #FFFF00>Lieutenants</color></b> are stronger, and have more attacks.<br><b><color #ff9900>Bosses</color></b> are the strongest and are particularly resistant to status effects. You may need backup when fighting a boss.<br><br><br>When you target an enemy or ally, you can note the difficulty of that target by the color of the name.</b><br><br><color DarkGray><b>Gray</b></color> names mean the enemy is quite weak and worth no rewards.<br><b><color LawnGreen>Green</b></color> and <b><color dodgerblue>Blue</b></color> names mean they are weak and give minor rewards.<br><b>White</b> means they are the same level as yourself and give normal rewards.<br><b><color #ffff00>Yellow</color></b>, <b><color DarkOrange>Orange</color></b>, and <b><color red>Red</color></b> names are enemies that are tougher than you.<br><br><b><color Magenta>Purple</color></b> names mean enemies that are vastly superior to you. If you train hard and hone your powers, you may eventually be able to take on purples."
// Page IdSayYouAre Text :
"P531328734" "Right.  Get yourself over to <color yellow>Dr. Steffard</color>, he'll tell you more about how to use your powers.<br><br>He's not far, just up the street to my right here."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - ReeseArrived 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page EnhancementGifting Text :
"P3423536153" "Hey new recruit, don't just stand there lollygagging. Can't you see we have a situation here?<br><br>Here are some <color lightblue>enhancements</color>, they'll increase your damage output a bit.<br><br>Get them slotted and we can get started."
// Answer Text :
"P51469715" "I'm ready now."
// Answer Text :
"P3441729447" "(Optional Help) How do I slot and use enhancements?"
// Page TeachEnhancements Text :
"P3246042684" "<color orange>Use these enhancements to improve your powers.<br><br>Click <color greenyellow>Enhancements</color> on the Powers Tray to see the enhancements you have. On that tab, click <color greenyellow>Manage</color> to go to the enhancement management screen.<br><br>You can put each enhancement on a different power, or stack them both on a single slot to get a slightly stronger one.<br><br><span align=center><img src=Tut_P_TwoEnhancements.tga>"
// Page AboutDestroyers Text :
"P684369163" "The Destroyers believe in only one thing: the strong make the rules. They've been getting more violent every day, but they are disorganized anarchists.  I'll probably be done with them by the time you get back out. The Resistance are using the Destroyers as pawns to destroy our beautiful city.<br><br>The Resistance are subverting members of our orderly society with their lies and propaganda, creating chaos and destruction among us. I need an insider to weed them out. That's where you come in."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P1905801903" "I'm going to send you to some of my associates.<br><br>They will teach you combat basics, and how to use your powers. Be sure to make good use of their expertise and they will teach you the skills you need to tackle whatever mission Reese might throw you into.<br><br>Are you ready?<br><br><color orange>As you go through the tutorial, you will see dialog options labeled <color lawngreen>(Optional)</color>. These options will allow you to learn more about the subject being taught, or more about the lore of Praetoria.</color>"
// AcceptString :
"P3010117077" "Yes, where to?"
// SendOffString :
"P3413263972" "First speak to Interrogator Hoffman.  He'll give you a chance to use some of your powers.<br><br>He's in the parking lot behind me, talk to him and he'll tell you about how to use your powers and gauge your opponents.<br><br><br><br><color orange>Your compass shows your current task, as seen here.<br><span align=center><img src=Tut_P_Interrogator.tga><br>Use <color lawngreen>Q and E</color> to turn until the marker is centered on your compass and follow the marker.</span>"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - P_Tutorial_Combat_Part1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// ActiveTaskString :
"P3915576416" "Talk to Interrogator Hoffman"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P4043768584" "I've taught you everything I know… well no, not really, but I'm busy now, go speak to the Interrogator.  I've got to stay here and send off the other new recruits.<br><br><color orange>Your compass shows the direction you need to go. Follow the marker to get to Interrogator Hoffman.<br><br>Additionally you can click the Mission tab on the compass to see information about current missions.  Selecting a mission from there will put that task on your compass instead.<br><span align=center><img src=Tut_P_Interrogator.tga></span>"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - P_Tutorial_Combat_Part2 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// ActiveTaskString :
"P1191853050" "Destroy a broken clockwork"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P2470097994" "Why are you coming to me, {HeroName}? Are those broken clockwork proving to be too much for you?"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P3416244743" "You have defeated a clockwork"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - P_Tutorial_Combat_Part3 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// ActiveTaskString :
"P2233425152" "Return to Interrogator Hoffman"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P595542252" "Why are you coming to me, {HeroName}? Doesn't Interrogator Hoffman still have something for you to do?<br><br><color orange>Your compass shows the direction you need to go. Follow the marker to get to Interrogator Hoffman.<br><br>Additionally you can click the Mission tab on the compass to see information about current missions.  Selecting a mission from there will put that task on your compass instead.<br><span align=center><img src=Tut_P_Interrogator.tga></span>"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - P_Tutorial_Combat_Part4 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// ActiveTaskString :
"P3665696640" "Talk to Dr. Steffard"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P1616282408" "Go and talk to Dr. Steffard, I've told you all you need to know from me. I've got to stay here and send off the other new recruits.<br><br><color orange>Your compass shows the direction you need to go. Follow the marker to get to Dr. Steffard.<br><br>Additionally you can click the Mission tab on the compass to see information about current missions.  Selecting a mission from there will put that task on your compass instead.<br><span align=center><img src=Tut_P_Compass.tga></span>"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P2430712211" "<color deepskyblue>Welcome to Praetoria</color><br><br>You look like a new recruit.  I have a few broken clockwork here for you to beat on.  Go for it.  Smash a few and come back when you're done."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - P_Tutorial_Combat_Part5 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P1629571925" "Excellent, I am glad to see your training went well. I think Reese is ready for you now, or I should say that you are ready for Reese."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskBegin 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// RandomFameString :
"P4165755592" "I hear {HeroName} has just joined the Powers Division!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - P_Tutorial_DoorMission 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Earpiece 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P1326590023" "Earpiece"
// DetailString :
"P3920357812" "The Resistance Clockwork gave you a small earpierce. There are some loose wires on certain parts of the device, but it looks like it should work."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - ClockworkKilled 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P1640321987" "Clockwork Retrieved"
// DetailString :
"P483043590" "A few moments after the Clockwork leaves the warehouse, you receive information on your PDA from Reese, saying that they have captured the Clockwork you sent up and are in the process of retrieving information from it.<br><br>Reese reports back shortly afterwards that they were able to discover the location of a Resistance base from that Clockwork. A squad of PPD are now on their way to the hideout."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - ChoseResistance 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P1759356978" "The Resistance"
// DetailString :
"P2926153087" "Despite being sent into the tunnels to arrest a member of the Resistance, you chose to side with them, freeing the man who guided you through the ghoul-infested tunnels."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - ChoseLoyalist 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P574377745" "The Loyalists"
// DetailString :
"P2108565840" "You fulfilled the mission that Reese sent you on, putting down the member of the Resistance you were sent in to find."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - DialogTree 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page NoHeal Text :
"P642927368" "<color slategray>LoA.dIn.G[pRE.rec.MSG] // reLAyinG Me$$^&!</color><br><br>Greetings, {HeroName}. I am a-a-a-a Clockwork programmed t-t-to aid the Resistance. <br><br>The ma-ma-ma-ma-ma-person you are to meet is currently on the r-r-r-run from the PPD. I have been se-se-se-sent to sp-sp-sp...<br><br><color slategray>buF[msg]; nop; mSg=buf // buffERinG meSS^%1</color><br><br>Please use the supply crate to retrieve a-a-a-a-a... some inspirations."
// Answer Text :
"P3936123470" "Alright."
// Answer Text :
"P3462583435" "(Optional) I don't understand half of what you are saying."
// Answer Text :
"P4178370567" "(Optional Help) Wait, how do I use the supply crate?"
// Page HowToClickie Text :
"P2556909079" "<color orange>Some missions have an objective to find one or more <color yellow>'glowies'</color> within the map. Glowies glow and give off a humming sound. You activate the glowie by left-clicking it.<br><br>Activate the crate glowie to retrieve your inspirations.</color>"
// Answer Text :
"P931464863" "Ah. Gotcha."
// Page ClockworkSpeek Text :
"P723386422" "<color slategray>PrS(Que.rY[TgT.cuR]) == ErRRor // miSMat[- er570</color><br><br>Errror.  P-please re-re-re-re-re<br><br><color slategray>buF[msg]; nop; mSg=buf // buffERinG meSS^%1</color><br><br>REstaTE youR stateMeNT as A QuesTION, plEASE."
// Answer Text :
"P585224762" "Umm... Nevermind."
// Answer Text :
"P4049229481" "(Optional) Why do you speak strangely?"
// Page ClockworkSpeekToo Text :
"P2400501190" "Acknowledged.<br><br>This clockwork has been programmed with several pre-recorded messages to better interface with end users.  Unfortunately due to some of the <color dodgerblue>upgrades</color> this clockwork has re-received, the playback mechanism has been damaged, so some skip-skipping is inevitable."
// Answer Text :
"P613485974" "Wait, no.  I meant the OTHER language.  The recorded messages I understand.  Mostly."
// Answer Text :
"P2603764861" "Yeah. You know what? Just forget it."
// Answer Text :
"P2062520445" "(Optional) Ummm... '?CWK.SPK != CIT.SPK'"
// Page ClockworkSpeekFour Text :
"P584739795" "<color slategray>LoA.dIn.G[rDa.taB.aSe] // enCylopedIA M0!]#</color><br><br><color red>The creator</color> of the clockwork intended them to be easy to t-t-troubleshoot, debug, and to interact with.<br><br>Clockwork are built with an audio feedback system that is integrated with the processing module of the clockwork so that whenever the clockwork ch-ch-changes tasks, they will give audio feedback of what the new task is, in a language very s-s-similar to their own internal machine code."
// Answer Text :
"P879327088" "Ah.  Hm... 'CWK[TSK] = FIN.'"
// Answer Text :
"P3787048031" "(Optional) Wait, how do I use the supply crate?  Errr... '?INT(TGT.OBJ[SPL.CRA])'"
// Page Heal Text :
"P3441658824" "DEPRECATED<color deepskyblue>Welcome to Praetoria</color><br><br>You have co-co-collected an inspiration, now you have to use it in order to heal.<br><br>Inspirations: <color orange>Click on the Inspiration text above your powers tray. This will open a small window where you will see a green health inspiration. Clicking the health inspiration will heal your character.<br><br><span align=center><img src=Tut_P_TrayWInspn.tga></span>"
// Answer Text :
"P3431942317" "Hold on, let me use this inspiration..."
// Answer Text :
"P1800374379" "Okay, I've healed... Now what?"
// Page Heal2 Text :
"P425395864" "DEPRECATED<color deepskyblue>Welcome to Praetoria</color><br><br>You have co-co-collected an inspiration. I would advise w-w-waiting to use that when the time is right - it will increase your damage for a short amount of time.<br><br>Inspirations: <color orange>Click on the Inspiration text above your powers tray. This will open a small window where you will see a red power inspiration. Clicking the power inspiration will increase your character's damage for a short period of time.<br><br><span align=center><img src=Tut_P_TrayWInsp.tga></span>"
// Answer Text :
"P2136981924" "Okay, now what?"
// Page Healed Text :
"P1664588919" "Here, please ta-take this earpiece. The man you are su-supposed to meet with will speak with you through it.<br><br>I have been instructed to give you additional data if required."
// Answer Text :
"P4231960085" "I'm ready to get moving. What's next?"
// Answer Text :
"P4268280258" "(Optional) I'd like a better idea of what's going on here."
// Answer Text :
"P2685129313" "(Optional Help) Tell me how Inspirations work."
// Page HowToInspirations Text :
"P942443127" "<color orange>Click on the Inspirations text on your powers tray to open your inspirations window. You can right-click inspirations to learn about them, and left-click to activate them.<br><br>You have a Righteous Rage and a Resurgence. Righteous Rage will increase your damage output for 60 seconds, while the Resurgence will heal you a great deal. Inspirations are single-use only. There are several kinds of inspirations.<br><br><span align=center><img src=Tut_P_TrayWInsp.tga></span>"
// Page Door Text :
"P1456149131" "G-good l-l-luck, {HeroName}."
// Page Info Text :
"P3230904648" "<color slategray>LoA.dIn.G[rDa.taB.aSe] // enCylopedIA M0!]#</color><br><br>A-a-affirmed. First p-p-programmed s-s-speech a-a-alert launching.<br><br>The Resistance are a g-g-group of f-f-freedom fighters led by Calvin Scott. T-t-their goal is to b-bring down the t-t-yrant, Marcus Cole. H-he has taken away t-too many of o-our l-liberties in the n-name of peace. T-t-the f-f-final straw for the Resistance was the r-r-removal of the freedom of thought. A-a-all t-thoughts of the people of P-praetoria are now m-monitored by th-th-the <color yellow>Seers</color>.<br><br>However, once you join the Resistance, we will be able to protect your thoughts. Eventually, with Cole's de-destruction, the p-people of P-p-praetoria will be free once more.<br><br>Pl-pl-please tell me what else I can prop-properly inform you on."
// Answer Text :
"P3184447152" "(Optional) Tell me about Emperor Cole."
// Answer Text :
"P2980070641" "(Optional) What does your database say about Praetoria?"
// Answer Text :
"P3924943055" "(Optional) Tell me about the other Clockwork."
// Page Cole Text :
"P113042449" "Em-em-emperor Marcus Cole is the Emperor of the Earth. The hi-hi-history books have recorded that he has saved the world countless times over. It is said he has withstood a nuclear attack and has fended off <color red>Hamidon</color> with his bare hands. The pe-pe-people of Praetoria believe that he is a god come to show us the way to perfection.<br><br>He claims re-re-responsibility for saving Praetoria from the br-brink of total destruction and creating the ut-ut-utopia that it is today."
// Answer Text :
"P2691492907" "I'm ready to go"
// Answer Text :
"P2256304052" "(Optional) How does Cole keep the peace here?"
// Page Praetoria Text :
"P4289869671" "Praetoria is the ca-ca-capital city of Earth. It acts as the seat of power for the rest of the world.<br><br>It is broken up into a se-se-several districts. We're currently below No-no-nova Praetoria, the heart of Praetoria. This is wh-where Emperor Cole's tower is located. You can see the to-to-tower from anywhere in the city. Imperial City is the thriving business area you may have seen across the river before you came down here. Finally, there is Neutropolis which is where all the scientific research and de-de-development are done."
// Answer Text :
"P2550430720" "(Optional) Tell me more about the Resistance."
// Page PPD Text :
"P3630552448" "The Praetorian Police Department or the P.P.D. are Cole's po-po-police force that are given full authority to keep peace in Praetoria. The people are do-do-docile for the most part, so there is not much of a need for them on a da-da-daily basis.<br><br>There are several divisions of the P.P.D., such as the Powers Division, a gro-gr-group of beings with super powers. You were id-id-identified as a member of the Powers Division - ev-ev-every being in Praetoria who has heightened abilities mu-mu-must be registered with the Powers Division. <color deepskyblue>Praetor White</color> is in charge of the Powers Division."
// Page Resistance Text :
"P557350868" "<color slategray>Qry=reS; gEt.tru[haX.dat[rEs]] // feTcH trU!#</color><br><br><color slategray>DAt=chk; oVR.Wrt[dAT[rEs]] // datA OVerrrr!]#</color><br><br>The Re-re-re-resistance are a small group of people who believe that Cole's rule is not what it appears to be. Most Resistance members in Praetoria would be immediately recognized by the monitors topside, so must stay underground to avoid capture.<br><br>The Resistance fights for tho-those who have been run over by Cole's governmental machine, trying to help those who can't help themselves while att-att-attempting to change the government by any means necessary."
// Answer Text :
"P20907075" "(Optional) Tell me about the P.P.D."
// Page Clockwork Text :
"P1266235078" "The Cl-cl-clockwork are Praetoria's work force. We were in-in-invented and designed by <color yellow>Antimatter</color>. We do the work that others do not want to-to-to do. We are also used by the P.P.D. to help retrieve anyone they believe is going to be a problem. We ask no questions and do exactly as we're told.<br><br>Some Clockwork, like myself, have been repr-pr-programmed by the Resistance to serve their purposes."
// Page DestroyDoor Text :
"P3819895372" "I ha-ha-have been told to direct you to the do-do-door up ahead. You ca-ca-can destroy it to mo-mo-move forward. I will stay here in the me-me-me-meantime until events on the su-surface have calmed.<br><br><color red>You now have a choice</color><color orange> - you can choose to leave the Clockwork down here, or convince it that the PPD have cleared away from the surface. If the Clockwork goes to the surface, the PPD will scan it for all information regarding the Resistance, then destroy it.<br><br>These minor choices will appear throughout your travels in Praetoria. They will not change your alignment, but will affect the dialog and story.</color>"
// Answer Text :
"P2385719541" "(Leave)"
// Answer Text :
"P2317688301" "(Convince the Clockwork to go topside)"
// Answer Text :
"P125736061" "(Optional) (Convince the Clockwork to go topside)"
// Page Topside Text :
"P2295126205" "Understood {HeroName}, I will re-re-return to the surface. Thank you for your assistance."
// Answer Text :
"P3587735805" "Not a problem."
// Page PickedResistance Text :
"P1057880719" "Good to see you're on our side, {HeroName}, you're a real slammer huh? There's someone who wants to speak with you. I think you might've heard of him - <color yellow>Calvin Scott</color>. He's here now, near the entrance back to topside. You should go speak with him - he'll tell you what's gotta be done.<br><br>Good luck."
// Answer Text :
"P2587868253" "I'll go speak with Calvin Scott."
// Page PickedLoyalist Text :
"P1728885369" "You made the right choice, {HeroName}. Calvin Scott and his little band of subversives want only to tear down the utopia Emperor Cole has built for us.<br><br>Just remember, we don't <i>need</i> you here. The PPD has what it takes to bring down the Resistance - without the help from super-powered types like <i>you</i>.<br><br><color yellow>Provost Marchand</color> is coming down to speak with you - looks like he's taken an interest in you."
// Answer Text :
"P2100774194" "(Optional) What's your problem? I just helped you with that Resistance soldier!"
// Page MyProblem Text :
"P965627279" "The <i>problem</i>, {HeroName}, is that I don't like it when someone assumes they can do my job <i>better</i> than me. We all know that Cole is recalling supers from all over the world because he thinks the PPD are slacking off in bringing down the Resistance.<br><br>We're out to show you <i>and</i> Emperor Cole that the PPD have what it takes to stop this Resistance threat - even if we don't have your heightened abilities.<br><br>I'm here to keep my job, even if some other members of the PPD are slacking off. Got it?"
// Answer Text :
"P3755336280" "Easy there. I'd best go speak with the Provost before you say something you'll regret."
// Answer Text :
"P2534721268" "Back off, buddy. I see you've lost several men today, don't let it get to you."
// Answer Text :
"P403330983" "We are fighting the good fight together, officer. Remember that."
// Page ImResistant Text :
"P674587686" "You picked resistance... But I don't know that. However, I still don't trust you."
// Page ImLoyalist Text :
"P2682129929" "You're a Loyalist, which means I should like you. I don't. Deal with it."
// Page Fallback Text :
"P542885946" "What?"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - CalvinScott 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro Text :
"P171665434" "{HeroName}, good to see you. I'm the leader of the Resistance here in Praetoria. I'm pleased to see you're on our side - to be honest, I was a little nervous that you were going to turn on us."
// Answer Text :
"P2840620893" "Let's get to work."
// Answer Text :
"P1984806260" "(Optional) Why are you here talking to me? What are you doing here?"
// Page InformationPage1 Text :
"P614336683" "I usually try to be present when we get someone already registered with the <color yellow>Powers Division</color> to come on board. Most of our members who have super-powers are usually renegade - they can't be seen topside.<br><br><i>You</i>, however, are different. The Praetorian government sees you as a loyal follower. I want to use that to our advantage - since you've shown you want to help the Resistance."
// Answer Text :
"P626154003" "I'm ready to get working."
// Answer Text :
"P1375307439" "(Optional) How are we going to use that?"
// Page InformationPage2 Text :
"P1414694154" "I'm not too sure how gung-ho you were with the Powers Divison before, but now we need you to be all for it.<br><br>If you're going to do work for the Resistance, we're going to need Cole and his goons to believe you're on their side.<br><br>To that end, <color yellow>I need you to speak with Praetor White and work your way deeper into the Powers Division.</color>"
// Answer Text :
"P1161262865" "(Optional) So, I'm still to do the work of the Loyalists?"
// Page Loyalists Text :
"P2784806764" "Not exactly.<br><br>Once you've proven to Praetor White that you're a 'fine, upstanding member of the Powers Division', you can seek out members of the Resistance throughout Praetoria - maybe even normal folk who are sympathetic to our cause.<br><br><i>Then</i> you'll be able to fight the good fight. Just remember though, <i>you need to keep up the facade that you're with the Powers Division.</i> It's difficult, but we need a {Hero.gender=male man|woman} within the organization.<br><br>There is... another way you could help us, if you're interested in hearing me out."
// Answer Text :
"P3780741117" "I'll figure it out as I go - I'm going topside."
// Answer Text :
"P1769938361" "(Optional) What's the other way?"
// Page OtherWay Text :
"P3893502903" "We have plenty of people fighting the good fight, but only a few... insiders within the Loyalists.<br><br>We could use someone who works exclusively with the Loyalists. It'll be a dangerous job - and you'll have to be sure not to get caught. You'll probably have to do some... questionable things against us in order to gain the full trust of the Loyalists as well.<br><br>However, when you get to major operations, you can contact me. We'll figure out what you can do to turn the operation towards our favor.<br><br><color orange>You have the option, as a member of the Resistance, to do missions on the sides of the Loyalists. They will play through normally, however at certain points you will be able to contact Calvin Scott to add options to the mission in order to swing events in favor of the Resistance.</color>"
// Answer Text :
"P3393345752" "I'll think on it. For now, I'm going topside."
// Page Conclusion Text :
"P26031559" "Good luck then, {HeroName}. You'll want to contact Praetor White as soon as you get topside. Be careful around Praetor White, his cool exterior is just cover for his true nature: a marauder. He's brutal, cruel, and selfish. Show any weakness around him and he'll break you in half. You might not like it, but for now you'll have to put up with his attitude.<br><br>And remember, we need you as our inside {Hero.gender=Male man|agent} in Powers Division. Do what you need to do to gain their trust, but don't believe <i>anything</i> those Loyalist scum tell you."
// Answer Text :
"P1544711594" "I'll make sure to be careful."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - Marchand 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro Text :
"P3390137552" "Hello, {HeroName}. I am <color yellow>Provost Marshal Gerard T. Marchand</color>. I run all military operations for Emperor Cole - this means I also help run the PPD. <br><br>I'm impressed at your actions here today with the Resistance. Look around you, {HeroName}. All of these PPD died trying to get this one Resistance member. It's inefficient. I've done my best with the PPD, but it isn't enough.<br><br>We need people like <i>you</i> to help defend Praetoria against the Resistance, and other threats. <br><br>And believe me, there are <i>many</i> that would seek to destroy our beautiful city."
// Answer Text :
"P2860215001" "Right, look, let's just get moving. What's the next step?"
// Answer Text :
"P1123669436" "(Optional) What are these other threats?"
// Page Threats Text :
"P323198096" "Currently in Nova Praetoria we're dealing with the <color yellow>Destroyers</color>, a group of psychopaths who, as you may guess, wish to spread destruction amongst our beautiful city.<br><br>They are our top priority on the surface of Praetoria, next to the Resistance. We, of course, always have the threat of <color yellow>Hamidon</color> lurking outside of Nova, but our sonic barriers are keeping the beast at bay."
// Answer Text :
"P2723433343" "Okay, what's next?"
// Answer Text :
"P2362537516" "(Optional) Wait, what's a Hamidon?"
// Page Hamidon Text :
"P16828379" "You don't know?<br><br>Hamidon is a monster of pure malice. It nearly destroyed the <i>entire</i> world during the <color yellow>Hamidon Wars</color> in the 70s.<br><br>Emperor Cole is the only reason why we still exist today. He rallied the people of this land to fight the monsters of Hamidon and eventually faced off against the beast by himself.<br><br>Though Cole did not destroy Hamidon, he was able to push the monster back, allowing us the chance to rebuild civilization.<br><br>We're safe from Hamidon, for now, though it is a threat that still looms over us."
// Answer Text :
"P3003218789" "Interesting. So, what's next?"
// Page NextStep Text :
"P1897650066" "Exit through the door behind me and speak with <color yellow>Praetor White.</color><br><br>While I am in charge of Praetoria's military, he is the head of Powers Division. You'll be able to start you career in protecting Praetoria - or perhaps your rise to power - with him.<br><br>He is somewhat rough around the edges, but I fully trust him with the safety of our great city."
// Answer Text :
"P1139723102" "Sounds good."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - Marauder 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page ChoseLoyalist Text :
"P4120437140" "<color orange>Praetor White looks at you beneath his glasses, cracking his neck.</color><br><br>{HeroName}, heard a lot of things about you. Don't go getting all cocky just 'cause you took down some member of the Resistance. You're talkin' to the guy who fought durin' the <color yellow>Hamidon Wars</color>, so I ain't impressed hearin' that someone took down a stupid idealist who could use a gun.<br><br>But you got my attention, so that means something - for now.<br><br>You got some spark in you, even if you're still on the same level as most of the super-powered dogs here in Praetoria. Me? I'm the Top Dog, I keep all the other powered dogs in line.<br><br>You wanna get noticed, you break yourself away from the pack and join mine. That what you're trying to do, {HeroName}? "
// Answer Text :
"P1359950983" "That's the idea, Praetor White."
// Page InformationPage1 Text :
"P3653934899" "I see a lotta ambition in you, {HeroName}, but that ain't just give you a free pass into my group. <br><br>If you really wanna get through the Powers Division though, we're gonna have to make sure you've got the skills it takes to stand side by side with us. You think you've got what it takes? 'Cause I ain't got time to babysit any dogs when I could just throw you away."
// Answer Text :
"P4016204973" "I can handle whatever is thrown at me."
// Answer Text :
"P2033417013" "I've got what it takes, believe me. What's next?"
// Answer Text :
"P3956344654" "I delivered that Clockwork to you, didn't I?"
// Page InformationPage1Reese Text :
"P1571712547" "Tough talk now that you're with me, {HeroName}. Seems like you changed your tune from just a while ago. Reese told me how you were wantin' out of the Powers Division.<br><br>Seems funny that you're suddenly all gung-ho about it. Maybe you got wise, or maybe you got a trick up your sleeve.<br><br>All I know is that I'm gonna be keepin' my eye on you. You got some potential, talkin' to Reese like that, but we'll have to see if you've got what it takes to hold your own within <i>my</i> group in the Powers Division."
// Answer Text :
"P2742403230" "Alright, what's next?"
// Answer Text :
"P2641818225" "I delivered that Clockwork to you. I think that goes to show my potential - and my loyalty."
// Page InformationPage2 Text :
"P1031464273" "Hah! That's the spirit. Before we get underway, {HeroName}, there's something you should know.<br><br>There's a lot of stuff to be done here in Praetoria - keeping the peace and what not.<br><br>Once you prove yourself as a member of the Powers Division, you can either continue during work with the Loyalists, or you can go undercover into a Resistance cell. You'll have to do a lotta things for those scum in the Resistance, but it'll help us get some inside dirt on them - like wherever their main hub is.<br><br><color orange>You have the option, as a member of the Loyalists, to do missions on the sides of the Resistance. They will play through normally, however at certain points you will be able to contact a high-ranking official in the Loyalists to add options to the mission to swing events in favor of the Loyalists.</color>"
// Page ClockworkDelivered Text :
"P441180038" "That was you huh? Reese told me he was the one who tracked down that piece of tin.<br><br>Yeah, you did good on that. We found out the location of one of their bases with that piece of Clockwork. Looks like those punks have been snatching Clockwork from right under our noses to use for themselves! Maybe this little encounter will teach 'em to keep their grubby paws to themselves, at least 'till I get a hold of them to cut 'em off!"
// Answer Text :
"P323297320" "So what's the first step in all of this?"
// Page FirstStep Text :
"P1972475409" "Well, before we get underway, {HeroName}, there's something you should know.<br><br>There's a lot of stuff to be done here in Praetoria - keeping the peace and what not.<br><br>Even more though...we need to really strike at the heart of the Resistance. You finding that Clockwork for us, it helped, but those guys are like cockroaches. They're crawling all over the place and making things harder for us.<br><br>Once you prove yourself as a member of the Powers Division, you can either continue during work with the Loyalists, or you can go undercover into a Resistance cell. You'll have to do a lot of ugly things for those scum in the Resistance, but it'll help us get some inside dirt on them - like wherever their main hub is.<br><br><color orange>You have the option as a member of the Loyalists to do missions on the sides of the Resistance. They will play through normally, however at certain points you will be able to contact a high-ranking official in the Loyalist to add options to the mission to swing events in favor of the Loyalist.</color>"
// Page InformationPage3 Text :
"P1131999444" "Next huh?<br><br>We start working, that's what's next!<br><br>Get yourself used to being in the high society of the Loyalists, then come to me and we can get moving towards keeping the peace here in Praetoria.<br><br><color yellow>If you haven't already done so, speak with Praetor Duncan to level up and gain a new power!</color>"
// Answer Text :
"P2868661889" "Will do."
// Page ChoseResistance Text :
"P985742461" "{HeroName}, you think you're all that? You come walking up to me after botching that operation with Wrencher?<br><br>Now <i>I</i> have to explain to the families of those PPD that were down there why their husbands ain't coming back! You think I like trying to act all mopey to those punks?<br><br>You got a lotta work ahead of you if you're gonna get anywhere in the Powers Division. Tell me why I should bother putting you to the test to get to the next level!"
// Answer Text :
"P4099243237" "The operation was all over the place, I can do better with the next one."
// Answer Text :
"P4159134907" "I delivered that Clockwork to you, didn't I? That should prove something."
// Page NextOne Text :
"P644714577" "You're lucky I got an image to maintain, or I'd brawl you right here! Maybe you're right though, maybe you got some spunk to you, enough that you ain't running away with your tail between your legs with me yellin' at you.<br><br>Alright, {HeroName}. You got yourself a second chance to get into my little circle. But, you fail again, and you ain't just gonna be out to do whatever you want - you're gonna pay a visit to them other members of the Powers Division that are on 'vacation', if you catch my drift."
// Answer Text :
"P1707187524" "Drift caught, Praetor White."
// Page ClockworkDelivered2 Text :
"P368053352" "Yeah, you did get us that Clockwork, I'll give you that. Didn't think the Resistance were able to hack into our machines like that yet.<br><br>We got Reese leading a team now to one of them Resistance cells in the tunnels - that Clockwork had a bunch of data within that we were able to use.<br><br><i>Maybe</i> you got what it takes, {HeroName}. Maybe that operation being botched was cause those PPD weren't tough enough. We'll see.<br><br>For now, you got yourself that second chance. Report back to me when you're ready, cause your life is gonna change once you start working under me."
// Answer Text :
"P2786969114" "Will do, Praetor White."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - Rothstein 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page NotNow Text :
"P690287643" "Not now, {HeroName}, we've got ghouls!  {Hero.gender=male Throw in some muscle, soldier|Take down some chompers, missy}!"
// Answer Text :
"P2588408948" "Right!"
// Page Intro2 Text :
"P4240500004" "Whew, man, just our luck huh?<br><br>PPD chase us right into an old ghoul den! Sure hope that Wrencher is doing OK...<br><br>Anyway, the name's <color yellow>Rothstein</color>. You're that new {Hero.gender=male guy|gal} that we're getting from Powers Division, right? Good to have you on board to help us.<br><br><color orange>Despite talking face to face with a high-ranking member of the Resistance, you won't be able to bring him back to the Loyalists, given the sheer amount of support he has around him."
// Answer Text :
"P637445866" "Thanks!"
// Answer Text :
"P3498082413" "(Optional) Tell me more about the Resistance"
// Answer Text :
"P1721097898" "(Optional) What were those things? -Ghouls-?"
// Page Resistance Text :
"P2431715574" "I'll talk to you in <color yellow>plain talk</color> for now, don't wanna get you all confused.<br><br>Us, the Resistance? We're the last, best hope for humanity here in Praetoria. Cole's got all these people brain-washed into thinking that what he decides is best for everyone. But really, it's all just what's best for <i>him</i>.<br><br>Did you know folks can't own their own <i>guns</i> in Praetoria without having to sign up to join the PPD or Powers Division? It's nuts! Cole claims it's because, 'you don't need guns for your own protection when we're protecting you'.<br><br>Us in the Resistance, we're all about <color yellow>power to the people</color> and givin' it to them no matter what.<br><br>You wanna know about them ghouls too, or you goin' forward?"
// Answer Text :
"P2565996097" "Good to know. I need to get moving, though. See you around."
// Answer Text :
"P3093474117" "(Optional) Yes! Tell me about the Ghouls."
// Page Ghouls Text :
"P3192354213" "I'll talk to you in <color yellow>plain talk</color> for now, don't wanna get you all confused.<br><br>Yeah, we ain't really sure what they are. Some of the older guys in the Resistance say that they just sort appeared one day in the tunnels. Ever since then, we gotta be careful of where we go. You get ambushed by a horde of those things, you ain't coming back.<br><br>Those ghouls will <i>eat you alive</i> if they get the chance - they're nothing but a bunch of monsters. Some folks say that <i>we</i> made them, but seriously, what're we gonna use to make those monsters? I <i>wish</i> we could make ourselves an army of monsters to throw at Cole, believe me!<br><br>So you wanna know more about us, or you gotta be headin' forward?"
// Answer Text :
"P3741046858" "Right...well, I need to get going now."
// Page Ghouls2 Text :
"P2472627227" "Yeah, we ain't really sure what they are. Some of the older guys in the Resistance say that they just sort appeared one day in the tunnels. Ever since then, we gotta be careful of where we go. You get ambushed by a horde of those things, you ain't coming back.<br><br>Those ghouls will <i>eat you alive</i> if they get the chance - they're nothing but a bunch of monsters. Some folks say that <i>we</i> made them, but seriously, what're we gonna use to make those monsters? I <i>wish</i> we could make ourselves an army of monsters to throw at Cole, believe me!<br><br>You know somethin', nobody here really stops to smell the roses, y'know? I got a little somethin' for ya, {HeroName}."
// Answer Text :
"P2432280157" "No thanks, I'm good."
// Answer Text :
"P3985354570" "(Optional) What is it?"
// Page Resistance2 Text :
"P112545392" "Us, the Resistance? We're the last, best hope for humanity here in Praetoria. Cole's got all these people brain-washed into thinking that what he decides is best for everyone. But really, it's all just what's best for <i>him</i>.<br><br>Did you know folks can't own their own <i>guns</i> in Praetoria without having to sign up to join the PPD or Powers Division? It's nuts! Cole claims it's because, 'you don't need guns for your own protection when we're protecting you'.<br><br>Us in the Resistance, we're all about <color yellow>power to the people</color> and givin' it to them no matter what.<br><br>You know somethin', nobody here really stops to smell the roses, y'know? I got a little somethin' for ya, {HeroName}."
// Page BADGE Text :
"P2050733686" "Here, little token of appreciation, from me to you. Take it easy.<br><br><color orange>You just received a badge! Badges are awarded for various accomplishments. Some are easier to get than others. To see what badges you have, click on the word <color lawngreen>Badge</color> located on your <color lawngreen>navigation bar</color>.</color>"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P2198348007" "I need you to infiltrate the Resistance.<br><br>There are Destroyers all over the streets, it's a mess.  Don't be fooled, however.  They're just pawns of the real threat to peace in Praetoria: <color deepskyblue>the Resistance.</color><br><br>The Resistance is always looking for new recruits. I've made it known that you aren't happy being inducted into Powers Division. This should be enough to get your foot in the door. The rest is on you."
// AcceptString :
"P960773499" "Where should I go to find the recruiter?"
// SendOffString :
"P2230239304" "There's a Resistance recruiter that is ready to meet you.  Go to the door under the nearby underpass; that door will take you into the underground.<br><br>Once you make contact with the Resistance member, I will send in additional troops to arrest him and his buddies.<br><br>Be careful, the Resistance will tell you anything to get you to join them.  Don't fall into the trap of believing their lies."
// ActiveTaskString :
"P3285011465" "Welcome to Praetoria"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P1431132670" "You need to enter the underground, I will send in backup once you make contact.<br><br><color orange>Follow the marker on your compass to the underground entrance.  If the marker gets deselected, you can reselect it by clicking on the mission tab, then selecting the mission from Reese."
// TaskTitle :
"P1699820170" "<color gold>Welcome to Powers Division</color>"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// MissionDef 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// EntryString :
"P3988328511" "You've made your way into the den where the Resistance are. Up ahead, you can hear the sound of a Clockwork repairing itself."
// Script Variable BOSS_DISPLAYNAME :
"P3383608100" "Nothing"
// Script Variable Greeting :
"P2275253406" "Hello there son"
// Script Variable SaysList :
"P3149943563" "<t=4 caption x= 0.2 y=0.3 d=4><scale 1.75><color white><bgcolor SlateGray>Yo, {HeroName}, it's Wrencher, the guy you're meeting with.<t=5 caption x= 0.3 y=0.3  d=5><scale 1.75><color white><bgcolor SlateGray>We got a problem, PPD chased us right into a den of ghouls! Our boys could use your help!"
// Script Variable SaysList :
"P3284642018" "<t=6 caption x= 0.2 y=0.3 d=6><scale 1.75><color white><bgcolor SlateGray>See down there? That's day to day in the tunnels, trying our best not to get chomped.<t=6 caption x= 0.3 y=0.3  d=6><scale 1.75><color white><bgcolor SlateGray>We get out of here fast enough, we can scamp and let them PPD badgers and Ghouls chomp - wha?! Hold on, {HeroName}, we're under attack! It's the PPD!"
// Script Variable SaysList :
"P3793101891" "<t=4 caption x= 0.6 y=0.5 d=4><scale 1.75><color white><bgcolor SlateGray>PPD found us, {HeroName}, watch out!<t=5 caption x= 0.3 y=0.3  d=5><scale 1.75><color white><bgcolor SlateGray>You might run into a few of 'em yourself up ahead!"
// Script Variable SaysList :
"P2355477643" "<t=4 caption x= 0.7 y=0.3 d=4><scale 1.75><color white><bgcolor SlateGray>Ugh! Hey give that radio ba-!"
// Script Variable SaysList :
"P1554719535" "<t=6 caption x= 0.2 y=0.3 d=6><scale 1.75><color white><bgcolor SlateGray>Word on the street is that you ain't too pleased with being part of the Powers Division.<t=6 caption x= 0.3 y=0.3  d=6><scale 1.75><color white><bgcolor SlateGray>We could use more folks like you, people willin' to talk back to them guys in power. We meet up, we can - wha?! Hold on {HeroName}, it's the PPD!"
// Script Variable SaysList :
"P3793214176" "I'm dead!"

